stdout ---
Make your json look really good

Usage: jjp format [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --mode <MODE>
          Pretty print, or remove all insignificant whitespace (uglify, also known as minify). --mode uglify cannot be combined with --parser jsonlines or --preferred-width [default: pretty] [possible values: pretty, uglify]
  -u, --uglify
          Shorthand for --mode uglify. --mode uglify cannot be combined with --parser jsonlines or --preferred-width
      --preferred-width <PREFERRED_WIDTH>
          Preferred maximum line width. Note this is not a hard maximum width. --preferred-width cannot be combined with --parser jsonlines or --mode uglify [default: 80]
      --end-of-line <END_OF_LINE>
          Line ending to use when formatting output [default: lf] [alias: --eol] [possible values: lf, crlf]
      --parser <PARSER>
          Parser to use for input. --parser jsonlines cannot be combined with --mode uglify or --preferred-width [default: json] [possible values: json, jsonlines]
  -h, --help
          Print help

Examples:
	$ echo -en "{ \"rust\":\"is a must\"   } " | jjp format
	{ "rust": "is a must" }

	$ echo -en "{ \"shoppingList\": [\"cheese\", \"slushy machine\"]   } " | jjp format --uglify
	{"shoppingList":["cheese","slushy machine"]}

